{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And the day-hawk after its kind.</b> The (day-hawk) mentioned here includes many species, all of which are of the kind of ayah; and you will find that our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Ḥullin 63b) that one hundred twenty species of birds were known to them, all of them of the kind of ayah, and it is possible that there are still more like these. And likewise in the kind of raven, many and many will be found, even though they are not identical and their name is changed — as the white Sinai-raven (Torat Kohanim; Ḥullin 62b), which is a kind of raven."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:55:17.839864903Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}